<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14838" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dŭcātus</span></b> ,
		ūs, m.
		dux, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>military leadership</i>, <i>command</i> =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡγεμονία</span> (post-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Tib. 19</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 21, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 2,
				15, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sirach, 7, 4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calculis omnibus ducatum latrones ei deferunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 7, p. 191 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			gen., <i>guidance</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caecus autem si caeco ducatum praestet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Matt. 15, 14</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>authority</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quaerere a domino ducatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sir. 7, 4 al.</span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
